      "math_academy_id": "e-14424",
      "problem": "Use the model below to calculate $\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/8eccf163bffabb43593188590a1f995544f3d1ac0aebcdd87dce638b230f8165.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Since we need to divide by $\\color{blue}4$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/a34a3fb198ef2ea79f8baf8f0acbdbdc179c6259c614824315d3d96e5ea4e921.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4 = \\dfrac{1}{16}\\,.\n$$",
